{"id":"mahabharata-10-011","work":"mahabharata","part":10,"partName":"सौप्तिकपर्व","partNameEn":"Sauptika Parva","unit":11,"title":"एकादशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 11 · Draupadi's grief and vow","summary":{"en":"Draupadi, learning of her sons' death, sits fasting until she gets the jewel from Ashvatthaman's head, and she asks Bhima to avenge her. Bhima goes after Drona's son in his chariot and Krishna follows.","kn":"ಮಕ್ಕಳ ಸಾವಿನ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ತಿಳಿದ ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮನ ತಲೆಯ ಮಣಿ ಸಿಗುವವರೆಗೆ ಉಪವಾಸ ಕುಳಿತು ಭೀಮನಿಗೆ ಸೇಡು ತೀರಿಸಲು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಭೀಮ ರಥದಲ್ಲಿ ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮನನ್ನು ಹಿಂಬಾಲಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಅನುಸರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पुत्रों की मृत्यु जानकर द्रौपदी अश्वत्थामा के मस्तक की मणि मिलने तक उपवास पर बैठती हैं और भीम से बदला लेने को कहती हैं। भीम रथ में अश्वत्थामा का पीछा करते हैं और कृष्ण उनके पीछे चलते हैं।","te":"కుమారుల మరణం తెలిసి ద్రౌపది అశ్వత్థామ నుదుటి మణి లభించే వరకు ఉపవాసం ఉండి భీముని ప్రతీకారం తీర్చమంటుంది. భీముడు రథంలో అశ్వత్థామను వెంబడిస్తాడు; కృష్ణుడు అనుసరిస్తాడు.","ta":"மக்களின் மரணத்தை அறிந்த திரௌபதி அஸ்வத்தாமனின் நெற்றி மணி கிடைக்கும்வரை உண்ணாநோன்பு இருந்து, பீமனைப் பழிவாங்கக் கேட்கிறாள். பீமன் தேரில் அஸ்வத்தாமனைத் துரத்த, கண்ணன் பின்தொடர்கிறார்.","ml":"തന്റെ പുത്രന്മാരുടെ മരണം അറിഞ്ഞ ദ്രൗപദി, അശ്വത്ഥാമാവിന്റെ തലയിലെ രത്നം കിട്ടുന്നതുവരെ ഉപവസിച്ചിരിക്കുന്നു; ഭീമനോട് അവർ പ്രതികാരം ചെയ്യണമെന്ന് അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു. ഭീമൻ രഥത്തിൽ ദ്രോണപുത്രനെ പിന്തുടരുന്നു; കൃഷ്ണനും അദ്ദേഹത്തെ അനുഗമിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 10.11; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Fri Oct 30 2026","sections":[{"title":"ऐषीकपर्व","titleEn":"Aishika Parva (The reed weapon)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स दृष्ट्वा निहतान्संख्ये पुत्रान्भ्रातॄन्सखींस्तथा ।\nमहादुःखपरीतात्मा बभूव जनमेजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his sons, brothers and friends slain in battle, he was overcome with great grief, Janamejaya."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततस्तस्य महाञ्शोकः प्रादुरासीन्महात्मनः ।\nस्मरतः पुत्रपौत्राणां भ्रातॄणां स्वजनस्य ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then great sorrow arose in that great-souled man as he remembered his sons, grandsons, brothers and kinsmen."}},{"n":3,"text":"तमश्रुपरिपूर्णाक्षं वेपमानमचेतसम् ।\nसुहृदो भृशसंविग्नाः सान्त्वयां चक्रिरे तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"His eyes full of tears, trembling and senseless, his friends, deeply troubled, then comforted him."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततस्तस्मिन्क्षणे काल्ये रथेनादित्यवर्चसा ।\nनकुलः कृष्णया सार्धमुपायात्परमार्तया ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that very moment, Nakula arrived at the right time in a chariot bright as the sun, bringing Krishna, who was in utter distress."}},{"n":5,"text":"उपप्लव्यगता सा तु श्रुत्वा सुमहदप्रियम् ।\nतदा विनाशं पुत्राणां सर्वेषां व्यथिताभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She had been at Upaplavya when she heard that most unwelcome news of the destruction of all her sons, and was stricken."}},{"n":6,"text":"कम्पमानेव कदली वातेनाभिसमीरिता ।\nकृष्णा राजानमासाद्य शोकार्ता न्यपतद्भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like a plantain tree shaken by the wind, trembling, Krishna reached the king and, pained with grief, fell on the ground."}},{"n":7,"text":"बभूव वदनं तस्याः सहसा शोककर्शितम् ।\nफुल्लपद्मपलाशाक्ष्यास्तमोध्वस्त इवांशुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Suddenly her face, that of the lotus-eyed woman, was withered by grief, like the sun overwhelmed by darkness."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततस्तां पतितां दृष्ट्वा संरम्भी सत्यविक्रमः ।\nबाहुभ्यां परिजग्राह समुपेत्य वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then seeing her fallen, the agitated Vrikodara, of true valor, came up and held her in his arms."}},{"n":9,"text":"सा समाश्वासिता तेन भीमसेनेन भामिनी ।\nरुदती पाण्डवं कृष्णा सहभ्रातरमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Comforted by Bhimasena, the spirited Krishna, weeping, spoke to the Pandava, together with his brothers."}},{"n":10,"text":"दिष्ट्या राजंस्त्वमद्येमामखिलां भोक्ष्यसे महीम् ।\nआत्मजान्क्षत्रधर्मेण संप्रदाय यमाय वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune, O king, you will enjoy this whole earth today, having handed your sons over to Yama according to the warrior's duty."}},{"n":11,"text":"दिष्ट्या त्वं पार्थ कुशली मत्तमातङ्गगामिनम् ।\nअवाप्य पृथिवीं कृत्स्नां सौभद्रं न स्मरिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune, Partha, you are well, and having gained the whole earth, which has the gait of a rutting elephant, you will not remember Subhadra's son."}},{"n":12,"text":"आत्मजांस्तेन धर्मेण श्रुत्वा शूरान्निपातितान् ।\nउपप्लव्ये मया सार्धं दिष्ट्या त्वं न स्मरिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune, hearing that your heroic sons were struck down in that fashion, you will not remember them, while with me at Upaplavya."}},{"n":13,"text":"प्रसुप्तानां वधं श्रुत्वा द्रौणिना पापकर्मणा ।\nशोकस्तपति मां पार्थ हुताशन इवाशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard of the killing of my sleeping sons by sinful Drona's son, grief burns me, Partha, as fire burns its fuel."}},{"n":14,"text":"तस्य पापकृतो द्रौणेर्न चेदद्य त्वया मृधे ।\nह्रियते सानुबन्धस्य युधि विक्रम्य जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If today you do not, by prowess in battle, take the life of that evil-doer, Drona's son, along with his kin,"}},{"n":15,"text":"इहैव प्रायमासिष्ये तन्निबोधत पाण्डवाः ।\nन चेत्फलमवाप्नोति द्रौणिः पापस्य कर्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"then I shall sit here and fast until death; know this, Pandavas, if Drona's son does not meet the fruit of his sinful deed."}},{"n":16,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततः कृष्णा पाण्डवं प्रत्युपाविशत् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं याज्ञसेनी धर्मराजं यशस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the renowned Krishna, daughter of Yajnasena, sat down before the Pandava Yudhishthira, the king of dharma."}},{"n":17,"text":"दृष्ट्वोपविष्टां राजर्षिः पाण्डवो महिषीं प्रियाम् ।\nप्रत्युवाच स धर्मात्मा द्रौपदीं चारुदर्शनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his beloved queen seated, the royal sage Pandava, righteous in soul, answered the fair-faced Draupadi."}},{"n":18,"text":"धर्म्यं धर्मेण धर्मज्ञे प्राप्तास्ते निधनं शुभे ।\nपुत्रास्ते भ्रातरश्चैव तान्न शोचितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing dharma, auspicious one, your sons and brothers reached their end rightly, according to dharma; you should not grieve for them."}},{"n":19,"text":"द्रोणपुत्रः स कल्याणि वनं दूरमितो गतः ।\nतस्य त्वं पातनं संख्ये कथं ज्ञास्यसि शोभने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona's son, fair lady, has gone far away from here into the forest; how will you learn of his being struck down in battle, lovely one?"}},{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"द्रोणपुत्रस्य सहजो मणिः शिरसि मे श्रुतः ।\nनिहत्य संख्ये तं पापं पश्येयं मणिमाहृतम् ।\nराजञ्शिरसि तं कृत्वा जीवेयमिति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have heard that the son of Drona has a jewel born with him on his head. If I see that jewel brought after killing that sinner in battle, O king, and put it on your head, then I may live; that is my resolve."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा पाण्डवं कृष्णा राजानं चारुदर्शना ।\nभीमसेनमथाभ्येत्य कुपिता वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this to the Pandava king, the fair-faced Krishna, angry, went to Bhimasena and spoke."}},{"n":22,"text":"त्रातुमर्हसि मां भीम क्षत्रधर्ममनुस्मरन् ।\nजहि तं पापकर्माणं शम्बरं मघवानिव ।\nन हि ते विक्रमे तुल्यः पुमानस्तीह कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"You should save me, Bhima, remembering the warrior's duty; kill that evil-doer as Indra killed Shambara, for there is no man here equal to you in prowess."}},{"n":23,"text":"श्रुतं तत्सर्वलोकेषु परमव्यसने यथा ।\nद्वीपोऽभूस्त्वं हि पार्थानां नगरे वारणावते ।\nहिडिम्बदर्शने चैव तथा त्वमभवो गतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is known in all the worlds how in the greatest distress you were an island for the Parthas in the city of Varanavata, and again when Hidimba appeared you were their refuge."}},{"n":24,"text":"तथा विराटनगरे कीचकेन भृशार्दिताम् ।\nमामप्युद्धृतवान्कृच्छ्रात्पौलोमीं मघवानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too in the city of Virata, when I was sorely tormented by Kichaka, you rescued me from the trouble as Indra rescued the daughter of Puloman."}},{"n":25,"text":"यथैतान्यकृथाः पार्थ महाकर्माणि वै पुरा ।\nतथा द्रौणिममित्रघ्न विनिहत्य सुखी भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As you did these great deeds before, Partha, so now, killer of foes, kill Drona's son and be happy."}},{"n":26,"text":"तस्या बहुविधं दुःखान्निशम्य परिदेवितम् ।\nनामर्षयत कौन्तेयो भीमसेनो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing her many kinds of lament in her grief, Bhimasena, Kunti's mighty son, could not bear it."}},{"n":27,"text":"स काञ्चनविचित्राङ्गमारुरोह महारथम् ।\nआदाय रुचिरं चित्रं समार्गणगुणं धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He mounted a great chariot with a body of varied gold, taking a splendid, wonderful bow with arrows and string."}},{"n":28,"text":"नकुलं सारथिं कृत्वा द्रोणपुत्रवधे वृतः ।\nविस्फार्य सशरं चापं तूर्णमश्वानचोदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Making Nakula his charioteer, for the killing of Drona's son, he twanged his bow with its arrow and quickly urged the horses on."}},{"n":29,"text":"ते हयाः पुरुषव्याघ्र चोदिता वातरंहसः ।\nवेगेन त्वरिता जग्मुर्हरयः शीघ्रगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Urged on, those horses, tiger among men, swift as the wind and fast-moving, hastened along with speed."}},{"n":30,"text":"शिबिरात्स्वाद्गृहीत्वा स रथस्य पदमच्युतः ।\nद्रोणपुत्ररथस्याशु ययौ मार्गेण वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking the trail of the other chariot from his own camp, the mighty and unshaken one quickly followed the path of the chariot of Drona's son."}}]}]}